I chose to examine extreme heat and why Americans are moving based on the environmental risk. In looking at the Census Bureau in Maricopa County, Arizona it shows that it gained 46,866 residents from 2020-2021 and 33,305 in 2021-2022. Whats important about this information is that it shows that people are moving and relocating to this area rather than its population growing from births or immigration. Within this county Maricopa includes Phoenix where extreme heat is substantial. The NWS shows data that between 1991-2020 Phoenix averages about 111 days per year at above 100 degrees and 21 days at over 110 degrees fahrenheit. With this data it shows that Americans are not moving away from hazardous climates and rather that they are moving toward them. This however can be explained due to many economical reasons such as the potential tradeoffs that Americans are making for jobs, housing, and amenities. With this there are also technological factors such as air conditioning that helps stem this extreme heat. This causes the death rates and data because people may accept this exposure but are only able to because of technological and infrastructure advancements that reduce risk. 

